import {icon} from './app.js?v=6';
export function teacher(){return `<div class="page-heading"><div><h1>Teacher's corner</h1><p>EDUP3133 · Task 3 · Year 4 Science · Unit 4: Photosynthesis</p></div><a href="offline.html" class="btn secondary">${icon('download')} Printable trail</a></div><div class="notice"><strong>Before classroom use and submission</strong><p>Complete usability testing with at least two adults, record the changes, confirm lecturer approval for a custom website, and add your official cover details to the private submission. Do not publish identification numbers here.</p></div><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>Learning intentions and success criteria</h2><p>Pupils aged about 10, with prior knowledge that plants are living things and need water. English instruction; use partner talk and teacher explanation when needed.</p><ol><li>Explain photosynthesis as the process by which green plants make food.</li><li>Name all four needs and both products; distinguish water from food.</li><li>Make and test a prediction by changing one model condition.</li><li>Explain one way photosynthesis supports other living things.</li><li>Correct an inaccurate AI claim using two sources and remove private information before sharing.</li></ol><p><strong>Evidence:</strong> prediction, experiment log, two connected creek paths, evidence repair and privacy task, 5-question assessment (target ≥4/5), and written or spoken reflection.</p><p class="caption">Content alignment: 4.2 Photosynthesis, textbook learning-standard markers 4.2.1–4.2.5, printed pages 76–81. The supplied DSKP file is Year 2 and is not used as Year 4 curriculum evidence.</p></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>A 19-minute lesson sequence</h2><p><strong>Instructional design:</strong> Gagné's Nine Events of Instruction. <strong>Technology integration:</strong> TPACK, integrating accurate science, guided enquiry and interactive media.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>RPH phase / time</th><th>Pupil experience</th><th>Gagné mapping and evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Induction · 2 min</td><td>Plant mystery; predict where food comes from.</td><td>Gain attention, state outcomes, recall prior knowledge.</td></tr><tr><td>Explanation · 3 min</td><td>Choose the cartoon and guided playable leaf factory, or the original picture notes. Watch first, then send water, admit carbon dioxide and uncover sunlight.</td><td>Present content and guide learning.</td></tr><tr><td>Exploration · 3 min</td><td>Predict, manipulate one variable, compare model trials.</td><td>Elicit performance; give explanatory feedback.</td></tr><tr><td>Application · 3 min</td><td>Rotate channels and solve two water-routing puzzles.</td><td>Practise applying the water-to-root relationship.</td></tr><tr><td>AI investigation · 3 min</td><td>Inspect sources, repair a claim, redact private data.</td><td>Apply learning and receive feedback.</td></tr><tr><td>Assessment · 3 min</td><td>Five items, specific feedback, review links and retry.</td><td>Assess performance without a timer.</td></tr><tr><td>Closure · 2 min</td><td>Three discoveries, reflection and outdoor transfer prompt.</td><td>Support retention and transfer.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="caption">The two explanation modes are alternatives within the same 3-minute stop, not two compulsory activities. Timing is a design estimate, not a measured result. Flexible navigation supports revision; station completion records participation, not a formal mastery grade.</p></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>Two KPM AI-literacy domains</h2><p><strong>Pengajaran dan Pembelajaran (Teaching and Learning):</strong> pupils critically check a teacher-selected simulated AI response, consult two sources and repair a misconception.</p><p><strong>Etika AI (AI Ethics):</strong> pupils practise removing personal data, acknowledging AI assistance and crediting sources. The teacher remains responsible for checking content.</p><p>The brief allows simulated or teacher-selected AI output; pupils do not need a live AI account. Gamification is the contemporary technology used in the learning experience.</p><a href="https://www.moe.gov.my/surat-pekeliling-ikhtisas-kpm-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">KPM AI Literacy Guide and SPI Bil. 2 Tahun 2026 ↗</a></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>Media, inclusion and safe use</h2><ul><li><strong>CASPER:</strong> contrast for text and controls, alignment, simple instructions, proximity of labels to diagrams, selective emphasis and repeated navigation patterns.</li><li><strong>Multimedia:</strong> original illustration, text, controlled animation, optional speech and generated sound cues. Segmenting, signalling, coherence and spatial contiguity guide presentation.</li><li><strong>Access:</strong> keyboard/touch controls, reduced motion, larger text, low-data setting, transcript, printable alternative and no timed failure. Audio depends on browser voice availability.</li><li><strong>Privacy:</strong> no accounts, analytics, uploads or live AI requests in the app. Progress and reflection are device-local; explain shared-device clearing.</li><li><strong>Differentiation:</strong> read aloud, use paired talk, offer one-condition experiments; extend by explaining why a fair test changes one variable.</li></ul></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>Submission evidence</h2><p>The private project folder includes a seven-page documentation draft, source backup, an AI and asset log, and an adult usability-test form. Two genuine adult tests and their resulting improvements must be added before submission.</p><p>The separate third-person <em>The Last Leaf: Guardian of Greenhaven</em> game is planned for later. A future-game design note is included with the source; supplied 3D assets are not redistributed here.</p><a href="#credits">Sources, attribution and safety guidance</a></section>`}
export function credits(){return `<div class="page-heading"><div><h1>Explore kindly. Check carefully.</h1><p>Good scientists look after people as well as plants.</p></div></div><section class="safety-list"><div>${icon('shield')}<h2>Keep private things private.</h2><p>Never share your password, full name, address or a friend's photo with an AI tool. Ask an adult before using a new service.</p></div><div>${icon('search')}<h2>Check before you believe.</h2><p>Compare a claim with a science textbook or a named science organisation. An attractive picture or confident answer can still be inaccurate.</p></div><div>${icon('book')}<h2>Give credit.</h2><p>Say where ideas and pictures came from. Tell your teacher if AI helped. Do not pretend someone else's work is your own.</p></div></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>Where our science comes from</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><strong><em>Science Year 4</em>, Unit 4.</strong> User-supplied KSSR textbook, printed pages 76–81. Primary science content; ideas paraphrased and diagrams newly made. The full textbook is not redistributed.</li><li><strong>NASA Science. (n.d.). <em>What is the carbon cycle?</em></strong> Independent science cross-check. <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/kids/earth/what-is-the-carbon-cycle/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read with an adult ↗</a></li><li><strong>Kementerian Pendidikan Malaysia. (2026). <em>Panduan Literasi Kecerdasan Buatan (AI).</em></strong> <a href="https://www.moe.gov.my/surat-pekeliling-ikhtisas-kpm-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official guide and circular ↗</a></li><li><strong>NASA. (n.d.). <em>STEMonstrations: Photosynthesis.</em></strong> Optional teacher-led extension video; aimed at older pupils, outside the 19-minute core lesson. <a href="https://www.nasa.gov/stem-content/stemonstrations-photosynthesis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit NASA's video page ↗</a></li></ul></section><section class="activity-panel teacher-section"><h2>How this learning space was made</h2><p>Code, activity drafts and original garden and character artwork were created with assistance from OpenAI Codex and image generation. Science was checked against the supplied textbook and the linked NASA source. Final teacher review and genuine adult usability testing are still required.</p><p>The AI claim in the detective activity is an intentionally incorrect, authored simulation. There is no live chatbot. The garden character is fictional; its face is decorative.</p><p>Typeface: <strong>Nunito</strong>, under the <a href="assets/OFL-Nunito.txt">SIL Open Font License</a>. Icons and instructional diagrams are original SVG geometry. Sound cues are generated by the browser; read-aloud uses available device voices.</p><p>External links open another website, which has its own privacy terms. No external video is loaded automatically.</p></section><a class="btn" href="#map">${icon('map')} Back to my adventure</a>`}
